<!--
     Call recording.

     The LineageOS Dialer already has all the code
     (java/com/android/dialer/callrecord/), but it is off by default and, when
     turned on, records from the microphone.

     Here the source is 4 (MediaRecorder.AudioSource.VOICE_CALL), that is uplink
     plus downlink taken straight from the voice path, because this device
     exposes them. The proof is in /vendor/etc/audio_policy_configuration.xml,
     where "Voice Call In" is not only routed towards the speakers but also
     towards a dedicated input mix:

         <mixPort name="voice tx" role="sink" maxOpenCount="1" maxActiveCount="1">
             <profile ... channelMasks="...,AUDIO_CHANNEL_IN_VOICE_UPLINK,
                                            AUDIO_CHANNEL_IN_VOICE_DNLINK"/>
         <route type="mix" sink="voice tx" sources="Voice Call In"/>

     Should the recording come out silent, or with only one party, on some
     network or in some mode (VoLTE, BT SCO), fall back to 1 (MIC): it records
     the audio in the air from the microphone, so it always works, but only on
     speakerphone and at lower quality.

     Note: recording a phone call without the other party's consent is illegal
     in a number of jurisdictions. The feature is left to the discretion of
     whoever uses it.
-->
<resources>
    <bool name="call_recording_enabled">true</bool>
    <integer name="call_recording_audio_source">4</integer>
</resources>
